In a closed container, calcium carbonate and its decomposition products are in equilibrium: $\mathrm{CaCO_{3}(s) \rightleftharpoons CaO(s) + CO_{2}(g)}$ The forward reaction is endothermic.

State and explain what happens to the amount of carbon dioxide at equilibrium when

(a) the temperature is raised;

(b) the volume of the container is decreased, at constant temperature;

(c) the carbon dioxide is removed continuously by a stream of air, as in a lime kiln.
